<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:01:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Winners, losers, the EU: Five takeaways from the US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d865116738006cec3dde0a29e8b055821a264208acd9b8dcec1a6a524a8d84e9</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:00:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/winners-losers-the-eu-five-takeaways-from-the-us-midterms/a-79858901--d5d91689d3d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/winners-losers-the-eu-five-takeaways-from-the-us-midterms/a-79858901?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republicans suffered a crushing defeat in Tuesday's midterm elections, with the Democrats wresting control of Congress. What does this mean for US politics and the world?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>36 years later: Hungary opens Communist-era secret service files</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e8a785a7231840003eb7e8e0bc595db2b3ddf809687bb38690cf5aae3ba2d81</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:00:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T19:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/36-years-later-hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-service-files/a-79858016--dc09772faa12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/36-years-later-hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-service-files/a-79858016?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Decades after the end of Soviet rule, Hungary is releasing all its secret service files. The disclosure is sparking fresh debate about informants, guilt and responsibility.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kosovo: Outrage as authorities accused of not helping femicide victim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f31df5d13fac73cbe5f0a4c4efedc4c63dcabed0f051665f845d29576a3cefd</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:01:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-outrage-as-authorities-accused-of-not-helping-femicide-victim/a-79856726--34859fc77a44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-outrage-as-authorities-accused-of-not-helping-femicide-victim/a-79856726?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite reporting her husband to the police and pleading for protection, Arlinda Zekaj was brutally murdered. Now, thousands in Kosovo are protesting what they say is a dramatic failure of state institutions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's shifting role in the global drug trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:083d4eebf0d9af2d32c19688ca4659bfa59478fb264bf0d6495fd4a1938ab73e</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-shifting-role-in-the-global-drug-trade/a-79847720--a33472b9e48a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-shifting-role-in-the-global-drug-trade/a-79847720?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Recent discoveries of meth labs suggest parts of Africa are moving beyond drug transit and becoming sites of synthetic drug production.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What the Democrats' midterms win means for the US economy and Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5640416cff9f93bcd577b722d2e4e67bb0b366a4c0fb6787979a88bfcde57d84</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716--124f824b0e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From high oil prices and data centers to tariffs and mounting debt, economic concerns played a key role in the crushing defeat of President Donald Trump's Republicans. So can the Democrats now make a difference?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia deploys troops to Jakarta after wiretapping allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9748c49568d5d173753da607ddffb23df6aa9e23c47fc879269b026a7f3e0bf6</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779--6f55d522a605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indonesian troops are being stationed in Jakarta amid wiretapping allegations implicating the president's chief of staff. Suspects are being accused of illegally tapping the president's phones.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wawira Njiru, Kenya's school feeder and German Africa Prize recipient</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d1fcdcd8aa45a62a52e70fbffb70c3cb51c4d6acfe9897fea26cf2f858eb1c3</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:01:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wawira-njiru-kenya-s-school-feeder-and-german-africa-prize-recipient/a-79646537--47b719bb31e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wawira-njiru-kenya-s-school-feeder-and-german-africa-prize-recipient/a-79646537?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From a small fundraiser to a major enterprise, Wawira Njiru's Kenyan school feeding scheme has been more successful than she ever thought possible. She's now being awarded the German Africa Prize.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What US midterm elections mean for Ukraine, Iran and elsewhere</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31413dae1b22f3a46424b1b5b8e99b8f37d29cf170ee97c65b431591caf312fd</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T08:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-us-midterm-elections-mean-for-ukraine-iran-and-elsewhere/a-79836423--c94a74658887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-us-midterm-elections-mean-for-ukraine-iran-and-elsewhere/a-79836423?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republicans will no longer control the US Congress after the Democrats flipped both chambers in the midterm elections. The outcome could impact conflicts in Europe and the Middle East.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why South Africa's local elections matter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:312dca0f6cdb754ae4322ec8192a00a2659369a413cc355af12dfd8646d0a61c</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-south-africa-s-local-elections-matter/a-79842695--3bc8ee9505ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-south-africa-s-local-elections-matter/a-79842695?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Africans head to the polls on Wednesday amid water shortages, frustration with local services and questions over whether the ANC's support will keep falling.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China and India achieved diplomatic thaw. Now the border is flaring up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08f816c1f3f5b9dcfba91fae0484805ab31066beab567549134f8909b1577ff7</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-and-india-achieved-diplomatic-thaw-now-the-border-is-flaring-up/a-79843273--6b47f2ce5be9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-and-india-achieved-diplomatic-thaw-now-the-border-is-flaring-up/a-79843273?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indian authorities have confirmed a new border "face-off" between Indian and Chinese troops in Arunachal Pradesh, raising questions about the still fragile thaw in relations between New Delhi and Beijing.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Cyprus: From ties with Russia to a strategic alignment with the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8c2f84df758448e73c11d8ca6d0cfcc3e7c696a9d37dbfbf69ed2062fdc1ddb</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyprus-from-ties-with-russia-to-a-strategic-alignment-with-the-us/a-79841251--5a66c266e064.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyprus-from-ties-with-russia-to-a-strategic-alignment-with-the-us/a-79841251?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Republic of Cyprus long balanced ties between Russia and the West. Now, it is phasing out Russian weapons, expanding defense cooperation with the United States and redefining its place in the Eastern Mediterranean.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Houthi clashes near Taiz leave residents in a 'state of panic'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:416a6f249774943797af574c08f6438b1e5992e747d1e49e01e88cdf43823978</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthi-clashes-near-taiz-leave-residents-in-a-state-of-panic/a-79836913--fbc4d150c8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthi-clashes-near-taiz-leave-residents-in-a-state-of-panic/a-79836913?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fighting between Iran-backed Houthi rebels and Yemeni government forces has intensified around the city of Taiz. Residents face growing shortages of food, water and medical supplies as thousands flee their homes.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Multiple flights to European airports targeted by bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa9e4b515a9b94e1782f0f4b1921ff017e0bebb515c916a7b37d0442495606f0</id><updated>2026-11-04T22:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/multiple-flights-to-european-airports-targeted-by-bomb-threats/a-79842434--863c4364baea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/multiple-flights-to-european-airports-targeted-by-bomb-threats/a-79842434?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bomb threats involved two passenger planes bound for Warsaw, a Ryanair flight from London to Spain, two flights to Rome and a flight traveling from Israel to the Bulgarian capital, Sofia. No explosives were found.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
